dataType nameOfVariable = value;

value will decide the data type

Primitive Data Type [we don't need object to use them/we know in advance how much memory they will consume]
[byte, short, int, long], [float, double], char, boolean

Integer Number   --> [byte(127  to -128), short, int, long]
Decimal Number   --> [float, double]
single character --> char
Boolean Value    --> boolean




Non- Primitive data type [we need object to use them/we don't know in advance how much memory they will consume]
String, array.....